{
  "id": "ee1-12",
  "number": 12,
  "title": "Logic I: gates, truth tables and a half adder",
  "topics": ["Logic circuits", "Test and measurement instruments"],
  "goal": "Verify the truth tables of TTL gates with logic switches and a logic probe, then combine an XOR and an AND into a half adder.",
  "theory": [
    "TTL logic runs from 5 V. An input above 2.0 V reads as 1 (HIGH), below 0.8 V as 0 (LOW); in between is undefined. Outputs give at least 2.4 V HIGH and at most 0.4 V LOW.",
    "AND (7408) is 1 only when both inputs are 1; OR (7432) when either is; XOR (7486) when they differ; NAND (7400) is NOT-AND — and any logic function can be built from NANDs alone.",
    "Adding two bits A + B gives a two-bit result: the SUM bit is A XOR B and the CARRY bit is A AND B. That circuit is a half adder; two of them and an OR make a full adder.",
    "Every gate package needs its VCC (pin 14) at 5 V and GND (pin 7) at 0 V — a missing supply wire is the most common reason a logic circuit does nothing."
  ],
  "prelab": [
    { "key": "s11", "label": "SUM for A = 1, B = 1", "unit": "", "answer": "0" },
    { "key": "c11", "label": "CARRY for A = 1, B = 1", "unit": "", "answer": "1" },
    { "key": "n11", "label": "NAND output for A = 1, B = 1", "unit": "", "answer": "0" },
    { "key": "vih", "label": "Lowest input voltage TTL must read as HIGH", "unit": "V", "answer": "2.0" }
  ],
  "procedure": [
    "Load the reference build: LSA and LSB are the inputs A and B; U1 is a 7486 (XOR), U2 a 7408 (AND), U3 a 7400 (NAND). LED1 shows SUM, LED2 CARRY.",
    "Step through 00, 01, 10, 11 with the two switches. Touch the logic probe to each output (column 22, 32 and 42) and fill in the truth table.",
    "Measure a HIGH and a LOW output with the DMM and compare with the TTL limits.",
    "Pull out U1's VCC wire and watch what happens to SUM — then put it back."
  ],
  "table": [
    { "key": "voh", "label": "SUM output HIGH (A = 1, B = 0)", "unit": "V", "predict": "3.4", "source": "dmm:M1", "tol": 30 },
    { "key": "s11m", "label": "SUM for 11 (0 or 1)", "unit": "", "predict": "s11", "source": "probe", "tol": 1 },
    { "key": "c11m", "label": "CARRY for 11 (0 or 1)", "unit": "", "predict": "c11", "source": "probe", "tol": 1 }
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "kind": "truth",
      "label": "Half adder and NAND truth table",
      "inputs": ["LSA", "LSB"],
      "outputs": ["g22", "g32", "g42"],
      "rows": [
        { "in": [0, 0], "out": [0, 0, 1] },
        { "in": [0, 1], "out": [1, 0, 1] },
        { "in": [1, 0], "out": [1, 0, 1] },
        { "in": [1, 1], "out": [0, 1, 0] }
      ]
    },
    { "kind": "led", "label": "SUM LED lights for A = 1, B = 0", "part": "LED1", "on": true, "set": [{ "part": "LSA", "key": "on", "value": true }, { "part": "LSB", "key": "on", "value": false }] },
    { "kind": "led", "label": "CARRY LED lights for A = 1, B = 1", "part": "LED2", "on": true, "set": [{ "part": "LSA", "key": "on", "value": true }, { "part": "LSB", "key": "on", "value": true }] }
  ],
  "settle": 0.01,
